<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lạng Sơn</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Lang Son</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lạng Sơn is a city and province in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> on the main road and railway to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, near the Friendship Pass border crossing. For centuries it guarded the route of invasions from the north. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sino-vietnamese-war">Sino-Vietnamese War</a> of 1979 Chinese forces captured and largely destroyed the city before withdrawing, and it later became a busy centre of cross-border trade.</p></div>
